      "description": "Assistant Professor of Strategic Management & Entrepreneurship PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Assistant Professor of Strategic Management & Entrepreneurship Assistant Professor of Strategic Management & Entrepreneurship School of Business & Technology Search  2487- Posted October 12, 2026 The School of Business & Technology (SBT) at Emporia State University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Strategic Management & Entrepreneurship. Candidates should be prepared to teach a variety of management and entrepreneurship courses. Ability/willingness to teach online classes (including accelerated online classes) are required. The position is housed in the AACSB-accredited School of Business & Technology (SBT) and begins August 2027. This is a full-time, nine-month appointment. This position offers the successful candidate a choice between two appointment options: (1) a tenure-track appointment or (2) a non-tenure-track multi-year contract of up to three years. The successful candidate will be offered both options for consideration and may select the option they believe best aligns with their professional goals and interests. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach undergraduate and graduate students in Strategic Management, Entrepreneurship, Small/Family Business Management, Venture Creation, and other related subjects. Conduct and publish high-quality scholarly research in strategic management and entrepreneurship. Engage in service activities to support the SBT and the university with emphasis on program development and outreach in Entrepreneurship and Rural Entrepreneurship. QUALIFICATIONS: Terminal degree or anticipation of completing a Ph.D. on or before August 2027 from an AACSB accredited business program or closely related field. ABDs may be considered. Relevant teaching and/or industry experience. Excellent teaching evaluations. Evidence of high-quality scholarly activity. Demonstrated ability to maintain Scholarly Academic status based on Faculty Qualifications policy of the School per AACSB standards. COMPENSATION: Pay is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Compensation package includes a comprehensive benefits package. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), evidence of teaching excellence, and contact information for three references online . If ABD, provide contact info for dissertation chair. Consideration of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. A background check and official transcripts are required prior to hire. For more information: Contact the search committee Chair, Professor Payson Maydew, at: pmaydew@emporia.edu Emporia State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, parental status, or any other status protected by applicable law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
