    "https://hr.hornet365.com/director-for-integrated-communications": {
      "title": "Director for Integrated Communications",
      "description": "Director for Integrated Communications PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Director for Integrated Communications Director for Integrated Communications Marketing and Communications Search  2482- Posted September 29, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking a strategic, creative, and collaborative leader to serve as the Director for Integrated Communications. This position is responsible for unifying and elevating the voice of the university across all communication channels while advancing institutional priorities related to enrollment growth, brand reputation, public relations, and campus engagement. The Director develops and implements comprehensive communication strategies that support the university's mission and effectively engage prospective students, current students, alumni, faculty, staff, media, and community stakeholders. ﻿ Reporting to the Vice President for Engagement and Chief Marketing Officer, the Director for Integrated Communications serves as a key partner in shaping university messaging, strengthening brand identity, and ensuring consistent, impactful communication across digital, print, media, and internal communication platforms. RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and execute integrated communications strategies that support university priorities, including enrollment, advancement, academic initiatives, and institutional engagement. Lead cross-channel content development and ensure consistency of messaging, voice, and visual identity across all communication platforms. Collaborate with academic and administrative departments to promote university programs, events, achievements, and strategic initiatives. Direct media relations efforts, including writing press releases, pitching stories, responding to media inquiries, and building positive relationships with journalists and media outlets. Oversee digital communications activities, including social media, email marketing, website content, and other digital engagement strategies. Monitor communication analytics and performance metrics to assess effectiveness and guide continuous improvement efforts. Maintain and enforce university brand standards, messaging guidelines, and visual identity requirements. Support crisis communication planning and provide strategic communication counsel during sensitive or high-profile situations. Lead and support internal communication initiatives that engage and inform faculty, staff, and students. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: A successful candidate must possess a bachelor's degree in communications, marketing, journalism, public relations, or a related field. Candidates should also possess: Three to five years of professional experience in integrated communications, public relations, marketing, journalism, or a related field. Strong writing, editing, and storytelling skills across multiple communication formats and platforms. Experience working with media relations and digital communications tools. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects and priorities while meeting deadlines. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and collaborative communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in higher education, public sector, or mission-driven organizations. Experience managing university, corporate, or organizational brand strategy. Experience with crisis communications and reputation management. Experience utilizing communication analytics and data to drive strategic decisions. WORK SCHEDULE This is a full-time, 12-month position. Occasional evening and weekend availability is required to support university events and communication needs. COMPENSATION: Compensation will be negotiable based upon education & experience. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
    },
    "https://hr.hornet365.com/admissions-counselor": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Admissions Counselor Admissions Counselor Undergraduate Admissions Search  2464- Posted September 29, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking an energetic, student-focused professional to serve as an Admissions Counselor. This position plays a critical role in achieving the university's enrollment goals by recruiting prospective students, building relationships with families and school partners, and guiding students through the college search and admissions process. ﻿ Reporting to the Associate Director of Admissions, the Admissions Counselor serves as the primary contact for prospective students and families within an assigned recruitment territory. The successful candidate will represent Emporia State University through high school visits, college fairs, on-campus events, and individualized outreach while helping students discover the educational opportunities available at ESU. This position requires extensive relationship-building, effective communication, and a commitment to student success. Travel is required, particularly during the fall and spring recruitment seasons. RESPONSIBILITIES: Counsel prospective students and their families regarding the admissions process, admission decisions, transfer credit, academic programs, financial resources, and university services. Serve as the primary recruiter for an assigned territory, building and maintaining relationships with prospective students, families, high school counselors, and community partners. Represent Emporia State University at high school visits, college fairs, community events, and other recruitment activities. Participate in on-campus recruitment programs and admissions events designed to engage prospective students and families. Collaborate with Marketing and Admissions staff to develop and execute communication plans, including drip campaigns, calling campaigns, and other recruitment initiatives. Utilize CRM and enrollment management systems to communicate with prospective students and manage recruitment activities. Conduct daily admissions office activities, including individual appointments, phone consultations, presentations, and campus visitor engagement. Collaborate with campus departments to support enrollment initiatives and ensure prospective students receive accurate and timely information. Participate in professional development opportunities, conferences, workshops, and professional organizations as appropriate. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: A successful candidate must possess a bachelor's degree. Candidates should also possess: A minimum of one year of full-time experience in admissions, recruitment, higher education, or a related field. A valid driver's license or the ability to obtain one by the start date. Willingness and ability to travel extensively during recruitment seasons. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and familiarity with student information systems. Excellent interpersonal, presentation, organizational, and communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience using Target X and Banner. Full-time admissions, recruitment, academic advising, or transfer student experience. Experience working in a higher education setting. COMPENSATION: $48,000 annually. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
    },
    "https://hr.hornet365.com/college-access-coordinator": {
      "title": "College Access Coordinator",
      "description": "College Access Coordinator PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS College Access Coordinator College Access Coordinator Undergraduate Admissions – School Relations & Partnerships Search  2468- Posted September 29, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking an enthusiastic, relationship-focused professional to serve as a College Access Coordinator. This position plays a vital role in expanding access to higher education through high school outreach, student engagement, college readiness initiatives, and enrollment support. Working closely with students, families, high school counselors, educators, administrators, and community partners, the College Access Coordinator helps connect prospective students with opportunities available through Emporia State University, including Jump Start, Career and Technical Education (CTE) pathways, academic programs, and admissions initiatives. ﻿ Reporting to the Director of School Relations & Partnerships, the College Access Coordinator supports outreach efforts designed to increase college awareness and enrollment while helping students successfully navigate the transition from high school to higher education. The successful candidate will be an excellent communicator who enjoys building relationships, coordinating events, and supporting student success. RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide operational support for the University's Jump Start program and other college access initiatives by assisting students, families, counselors, and participating schools through established application and enrollment processes. Coordinate enrollment documentation, student follow-up, communications, and resources that help students successfully navigate enrollment and access opportunities. Conduct high school visits, classroom presentations, college and career events, and other outreach activities promoting Jump Start, CTE pathways, academic programs, and college access opportunities. Develop and deliver College 101 programming to help students explore educational pathways, understand the college experience, and prepare for the transition to higher education. Support and maintain relationships with high school counselors, administrators, educators, and community partners through regular outreach and engagement. Coordinate opportunities for ESU faculty, deans, and academic representatives to engage with prospective students. Maintain accurate records of outreach, student engagement, and enrollment activity utilizing CRM systems, institutional reporting tools, and other university technologies. Coordinate recruitment and enrollment materials, including admitted student packets, mailings, and student communications, ensuring information is accurate and distributed in a timely manner. Build and maintain relationships with alumni educators throughout the region. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: A successful candidate must possess a bachelor's degree in education, communications, business, student affairs, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of postsecondary education and relevant professional experience. Candidates should also possess: A minimum of three years of professional experience in secondary education, higher education admissions or recruitment, dual/concurrent enrollment programming, student success initiatives, or a related field. Experience organizing events and managing multiple projects simultaneously. Demonstrated success building and maintaining professional relationships with educators, administrators, community partners, or similar stakeholders. Strong communication, presentation, and relationship-management skills. COMPENSATION: $48,000 annually. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
