    "https://hr.hornet365.com/student-success-coach": {
      "title": "Student Success Coach",
      "description": "Student Success Coach PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Student Success Coach Student Success Coach Residential Life Search  2471- Posted September 17, 2026 The Department of Residential Life at Emporia State University is seeking applicants for the Student Success Coach (SSC) position. The Department of Residential Life strives to support the academic mission of the university by providing residents with assistance, connections, and opportunities to enhance their experience at ESU. The department is committed to the celebration of diversity, community safety, and student development. ﻿ As a member of the Residential Life Team, the Student Success Coach will promote and activate the mission, vision, and values of the department. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Residential Life, the SSC plays an integral role in enhancing student success and the overall experience of residents in assigned residential communities. Ideal candidates will be student-focused and possess the ability to build meaningful relationships, provide coaching and mentorship, communicate effectively, and support student success initiatives with exceptional attention to detail. This is a 12-month, live-on position that includes evening, weekend, and on-call responsibilities. RESPONSIBILITIES: Contribute to residential curriculum initiatives for assigned communities, including individualized and community support, educational experiences, and campus connections that enhance resident experiences and increase retention. Develop and facilitate workshops and seminars on topics such as study skills, wellness, and career planning. Encourage participation in campus activities, clubs, and organizations. Provide coaching and mentoring to help students establish academic goals, develop personalized action plans, identify strengths, and improve performance. Offer strategies related to study skills, time management, exam preparation, conflict resolution, and productive community behaviors. Serve as a member of an on-call duty rotation during evenings and weekends. Assess situations, provide initial crisis response and support, make referrals when needed, and assist with crisis management planning and follow-up. Ensure compliance with FERPA, Title IX, and Clery requirements. Assist students in navigating campus resources, including academic support services, tutoring, mental health resources, basic needs support, and financial processes. Provide information regarding academic policies, degree requirements, and registration procedures. Monitor student engagement and progress, maintain accurate records, provide timely intervention when appropriate, and collaborate with faculty and staff to support at-risk students. Support Residential Life and Division initiatives, including student staff training, recruitment and retention efforts, move-in, move-out, summer conferences, and other departmental programs and services. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders on behalf of Residential Life. ﻿ QUALIFICATIONS: A successful candidate must possess a bachelor's degree in education, communications, business, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of postsecondary education and relevant professional experience. Candidates must also: Reside on campus in a university-provided apartment. Demonstrate the ability to create spaces and relationships that support diverse student populations. Participate in a 24/7 on-call duty rotation and respond to campus within 10 minutes when on duty. Be able to work a flexible schedule, including evenings and weekends as needed. Successfully complete a background check. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Student Affairs, Education, or a related field. Experience with college housing, case management, crisis response, and student development theory. COMPENSATION: $43,403 annually. ADDITIONAL COMPENSATION Meal plan. Two-bedroom on-campus apartment. Utilities included. Internet included. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
    },
    "https://hr.hornet365.com/administrative-specialist": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Administrative Specialist Administrative Specialist Division of Enrollment Management + Student Success Search  2456- Posted September 17, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking a highly organized, detail-oriented, and customer-focused professional to serve as an Administrative Specialist within the Division of Enrollment Management + Student Success. This position provides advanced administrative and operational support across multiple departments and plays a vital role in supporting the division's daily operations and strategic goals. The successful candidate will be a collaborative team member who demonstrates professionalism, initiative, and a commitment to exceptional service while helping advance student success and institutional priorities. RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide advanced administrative and program support for multiple departments within the division. Prepare and maintain reports, spreadsheets, and other business documents. Assist with budget monitoring, financial tracking, and recordkeeping activities. Coordinate purchasing and payment processes while ensuring compliance with university procedures. Manage calendars, schedules, and meeting logistics for departmental leadership. Arrange travel accommodations and process travel-related documentation. Organize conferences, meetings, events, and special projects. Support human resources and payroll-related administrative processes. Supervise and support student employees as assigned. Serve as a resource for faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Maintain accurate records and ensure timely completion of administrative responsibilities. ﻿ QUALIFICATIONS: A successful candidate must possess a high school diploma or equivalent and a minimum of four years of experience in an office or administrative support position. A bachelor's degree is preferred. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree. Experience supporting multiple departments or operational units. Experience with budgeting, purchasing, payroll, or administrative operations in a higher education environment. REQUIRED SKILLS AND ABILITIES Successful candidates will demonstrate: Strong organizational and time management skills. Excellent attention to detail and accuracy. The ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Effective problem-solving and decision-making abilities. The ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with business software, spreadsheets, and office technology. A commitment to professionalism, confidentiality, and exceptional customer service. A positive, service-oriented attitude and dedication to student success. COMPENSATION: Compensation will be negotiable based upon education & experience. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
