    "https://hr.hornet365.com/director-of-student-health-services": {
      "title": "Director of Student Health Services",
      "description": "Director of Student Health Services PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS Director of Student Health Services Director of Student Health Services Student Wellness Center Search  2462- Posted September 9, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking a collaborative, innovative, and student-centered professional to serve as the Director of Student Health Services . This position provides both clinical and strategic leadership for the University's health care operations within the Student Wellness Center. The Director is responsible for delivering accessible, high-quality health services that support student well-being, academic success, and retention through an integrated approach focused on prevention, early intervention, student resiliency, and coordinated care. The Director combines direct patient care with leadership responsibilities related to clinic operations, staff supervision, compliance, strategic planning, assessment, and campus and community partnerships. Working collaboratively across the University, this role plays a key part in advancing a holistic and sustainable model of student wellness. ﻿ RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide direct patient care and clinical oversight, including assessment, diagnosis, treatment, prescribing, testing, care planning, and referrals in accordance with professional standards and applicable regulations. Lead day-to-day Health Services operations and ensure compliance with applicable federal and state regulations, laboratory requirements, professional standards, and university policies. Supervise, develop, and evaluate Health Services staff, including oversight of staffing, scheduling, professional development, and student employees. Establish strategic priorities for Student Health Services and support an integrated and sustainable wellness model. Utilize data and assessment measures to evaluate service utilization, outcomes, and effectiveness while identifying opportunities for continuous improvement. Collaborate with campus and community partners to promote health education, prevention initiatives, early intervention strategies, and appropriate referral processes. Participate in campus-wide initiatives focused on student health, wellness, retention, and student success. Oversee Health Services budgets, contracts, equipment, and other resources to ensure effective and sustainable operations. ﻿ QUALIFICATIONS: A successful candidate must possess: Master's degree in Nursing from an accredited institution. Current licensure as an Advanced Practice Provider or Physician eligible for practice in Kansas. National Board Certification. Clinical experience appropriate to the responsibilities of the position. ﻿ PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience leading or administering a college or university health service, student health clinic, primary care practice, or similar health care setting. Experience supervising clinical and/or administrative staff. Experience with health care compliance, risk management, and clinic operations. Experience working with college students or emerging adults. Experience using data and assessment to improve health services, student outcomes, and operational effectiveness. IDEAL CANDIDATE The successful candidate will be a student-centered health care leader who balances exceptional clinical practice with strategic and operational leadership. Candidates should demonstrate: Strong communication and collaboration skills. A commitment to prevention, education, and early intervention. An understanding of the relationship between student well-being, academic success, and persistence. The ability to build partnerships across disciplines and departments. Experience using data to inform decisions and improve services. A commitment to staff development, innovation, and continuous improvement in student health care delivery. COMPENSATION: Compensation will be negotiable based upon education & experience. BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit the benefits webpage . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references online . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
