    "https://hr.hornet365.com/2404---assistant-athletic-trainer": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Trainer PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS 2404 - Assistant Athletic Trainer Assistant Athletic Trainer Intercollegiate Athletics Search  2404 - Posted June 24, 2026 Emporia State University Intercollegiate Athletics is seeking to hire two Assistant Athletic Trainers. RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide athletic training services for Emporia State University’s intercollegiate athletic programs, including coverage of home and away practices and games. Give guidance to graduate level athletic training students in our accredited athletic training program. Conduct rehabilitation activities for injured student-athletes. Administer daily evaluations, preventative exercises, emergency care, treatments, and rehabilitaive sessions. Complete additional duties as assigned by Head Athletic Trainer. Keep accurate records of athletes' injuries, treatment, and medication. Ensure program records, medical histories, and insurance information is collected and organized. Serve as a liaison to team physicians, medical specialists, student-athletes, and parents. Manage the flow of information and answer questions. Work with physicians, other athletic trainers, and student-athletes to deliver comprehensive athletic training techniques and treatments, ensuring safety and high quality performance. Assist in the day-to-day operations of the athletic training room. Report necessary repairs as needed to ensure the athletic training facility is fully operational. Perform all other duties assigned by Head Athletic Trainer. ﻿ Compliance with the rules and regulations of the University, the NCAA, and the MIAA are of paramount importance. The overall responsibility of this position is for the successful operation of the program in full compliance with all such rules and regulations. As a condition of employment, the employee shall be required to participate in rules education programs offered by the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics. QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Physical Therapy, Athletic Training or a related field Must be certified by the National Athletic Trainers Association Board of Certification (BOC) Must have or be eligible for a Kansas Athletic Training License Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree in a related field 1 - 2 years of related professional experience COMPENSATION: Compensation will be negotiable based upon education & experience BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit here . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, and contact information of three references here . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual w