      "title": "Senior Power Plant Operator",
      "description": "Senior Power Plant Operator PASSWORD HELP FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS CLASSIFICATION AND COMPENSATION REMOTE WORK INSURANCE ENROLLMENT FACULTY VOLUNTEER EARLY RETIREMENT INCENTIVE Get in touch 555-555-5555 mymail@mailservice.com EMPORIA.EDU SEARCH STUDENTS EMPLOYEES FACULTY TECHSITE MARKETING + COMMUNICATION HUMAN RESOURCES FACULTY + STAFF OPEN POSITIONS 2397 - Senior Power Plant Operator Senior Power Plant Operator Central Power Plant Search  2397 - Posted June 18, 2026 Emporia State University is seeking applicants for a Senior Power Plant Operator position with our University Facilities Division. As a Senior Power Plant Operator, you will perform routine maintenance on various powerhouse systems, monitor automation control systems regulating building heating and cooling, operate high pressure steam boilers, and analyze discharge water tests. This positions work schedule will be 4:00pm to 12:00am with days to be determined RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform routine lubrication, cleaning, and rebuilding powerhouse instrument piping for steam, oil, water, air, and gas lines Record daily boiler logbook, record daily usage of steam, fuel oil and natural gas Monitor the campus building automation controls (STAEFA) that regulates heating and cooling Maintain high pressure boilers QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum Qualifications: Requires a High School Diploma or GED At least two years of experience in a power plant or similar environment Relevant safety training is required Physical Requirements Ability to lift 50 pounds frequently Standing or walking for 7 or more hours per shift Movements that require manual dexterity, trunk strength, wrist-finger movement, twisting, bending, pushing, and pulling. COMPENSATION: Compensation will be negotiable based upon education & experience BENEFITS: Base pay is one component of Emporia State University’s total rewards package. We are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family that include: Health Insurance Free Dental insurance for employees Retirement through the Kansas Board of Regents Paid parental leave Up to 31 days paid vacation and holiday days Tuition reduction and tuition assistance Dependent tuition waiver For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit here . APPLY: Please upload a cover letter, resume, contact information of three references and a ESU Application here . Consideration of applications will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. A background check is required prior to hire. For more information Human Resources humres@emporia.edu (620) 341-5379 Emporia State University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, race, color, national origin, ethnicity, religion, gender, sex, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, parental status, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as an individual with a disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other factors which cannot be considered by law. About ESU Employee Benefits Employment Notices EMPORIA STATE UNIVERSITY 1 Kellogg Circle, Emporia, KS  66801 Questions? Please contact the IT Help Desk (620)341-5555 or helpdesk@emporia.edu Share by:"
